# Driftbank Ford -- vertical river route, 14x36 (buffer 840/1300). Build: python3 amap2.py driftbank_ford.amap
#
# HOOK: meltwater from Mt. Mortar runs the whole length of the route. You walk it on foot and
#   cross on three driftwood log bridges, or you Surf it: drop in at the inlet, cross the pool
#   and ride the current under the bridges to the bottom. Surf is optional. It opens an island,
#   two Swimmers and a fast way down.
# BEATS (N to S):
#   1. North gate (from Hearthhollow's south stub). The river comes out of a gorge between two
#      mesas, and rapids (8e/8f, WATERFALL collision) make it downstream-only for surfers.
#   2. Bridge 1 takes you to the west bank. A Cut tree (5b) under the cliff guards an item nook.
#   3. West bank: a 1-wide path past grass pockets (Fisher, Camper). A notch in the bank (block
#      58) is the Surf inlet into the Ford Pool, which is 5 wide with an island item and
#      SwimmerM/F.
#   4. East-bank ledge cascade: three ledge rows (56/56/57) give a one-way southbound shortcut
#      that skips bridges 1 and 2. A Picnicker stands between the ledges. Northbound walkers
#      must take the bridges.
#   5. Bridge 2 takes you back east. Then the river steps east twice (87/86 + a1/a5 lips),
#      Fisher2 and a Bird Keeper squeeze the east bank, and Bridge 3 takes you west to the
#      south exit.
#   6. The DriftCollector NPC on the lower east bank keeps what floats downstream: one random
#      item a day (a cheap daily hook that also fits the no-Pokemon-Center item economy).
# TRAINERS: Fisher, Camper, Picnicker, SwimmerM, SwimmerF (Surf), Fisher2, BirdKeeper.
# ITEMS: cut_nook_item (Cut), island_item (Surf), hidden_top, hidden_bank, daily drift item.
# BRIDGES: the grid uses 89 (deck, FLOOR with UP/DOWN walls), i.e. the walk-over state. In
#   game, copy Route45's two-scene system: the .ablk ships 98/99 (surf-under) and
#   changebridgeblock swaps all 3 bridges (6 blocks) between 98/99 and 89 on step triggers.
#   Checked both ways. Deck state: N<->S walkable. Surf-under state: from the inlet,
#   the whole river from the top edge to the bottom edge is surfable.
# PLACEMENT: N = Hearthhollow's S stub (concept 2). S = Pinefall Lake Campsite (concept 6) or
#   Orchard Road's S stub. The river leaves the bottom edge at cols 6-7 and the rapids touch
#   the top edge, so the neighbours need matching water (or end it in a lake).
#   ref Route42 (Mortar-area palette).
# GAPS: no stepping-stone / shallow-ford block exists (0a in water is WALL), so the "fords"
#   are log bridges. The island is 58/59/76 shores around a grass block with a flush top,
#   like vanilla's flush water.
ref Route42
key m=71 y=68 z=69 Y=6a 7=70 9=6b c=6c k=72 d=6d e=6e f=6f
key L=88 R=8a W=8e V=8f B=89 G=87 H=86 -=85 J=84 K=8b N=8c D=8d A=a8
key p=a0 q=a1 u=a2 P=a4 Q=a5 U=a6
key 5=5b
